Building ucsd-psystem-vm
========================

The virtual machine is built by the top-level Makefile of the UCSD-P-System
repository; see README.md there.

Requirements:

    C compiler
    SDL3             Optional.  The console window (text and Turtle
                     Graphics) and ucsdpsys_turtleserver; build with SDL=no
                     to skip them.
    curses           Optional.  The terminal console (ncurses on most
                     systems); build with CURSES=no to skip it.

At least one of SDL3 and curses is needed to use the system interactively;
batch mode (-b) needs neither.

The console window's font is pre-rendered from DejaVu Sans Mono into
ucsdpsys_vm/console_font.h.  To change it, run ucsdpsys_vm/console_font.py
(needs Python 3 and Pillow); see the comment at its top.

libexplain is not needed: a small stand-in is bundled in
subprojects/libexplain.

disk-images/ contains two UCSD P-System disk images that run on the VM.  Peter
Miller included these in his ucsd-psystem-os project, but they are included here
to make this project self-sufficient.

Peter Miller's original build instructions (X11, autoconf) are kept, for
history, in etc/building.man.
